{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Explore the codebase at /home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue to understand how Vue rendering currently works. I need to understand:\n\n1. The TypeScript/JS side: How Vue components are mounted, updated, and destroyed in the LiveView hooks. Look at assets/hooks.ts, assets/index.ts, and any related files.\n2. The Vite plugin: How components are discovered and registered (assets/vitePlugin.js)\n3. The Elixir side: How components are rendered server-side (lib/live_vite/components.ex, lib/live_vite/ssr/)\n4. Any existing abstractions or patterns that could inform a renderer interface\n\nPlease read the full contents of these key files and provide a detailed summary of:\n- How Vue apps are created and mounted\n- How props are passed and updated\n- How SSR works\n- How the hook lifecycle (mounted, updated, destroyed) maps to Vue lifecycle\n- Any Vue-specific code that would need to be abstracted for other frameworks\n\nAlso check if there's a reference to a React/Astro project at /home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro that might show how a React renderer could look."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0186sJbD2wUdJtBvguBQXVMf","session_id":"f7614b6c-f448-43a7-8572-6bc7e0743cbe","uuid":"cb68b2bc-f036-4b5c-91b7-a840ab56bdbb"}
